  "verdict": "PARTIAL / FRONTIER-CONFIRMED. p 0.25 pushes further along the resample frontier: pp-reliance dP 0.187->0.122 and baseline switch mass 0.404->0.343 (offline, identical v7 states); live loop DEPTH shrinks (bc_vs_heuristic max_switch_run 29->21; bc_vs_random 73->14) and bc_vs_random win jumps 0.3->0.9. BUT the core loop is NOT broken: both arms stay c_pathological, ping_pong flat (~0.53->0.55 heuristic, ~0.54->0.62 random) despite pp-reliance halving again, and bc_vs_heuristic win stays 0.0.",
  "decision_rule_outcome": "Closest to pre-registered Outcome 2 (resample lever capping on the core loop), refined: the pp-CARRIED long-run component keeps responding to resample strength (max_switch_run down, random win up), but the residual short PING-PONG (A->B->A) is pp-INDEPENDENT -- its rate does not move as dP halves. Pushing pp-reliance lower (more resample OR an encoder pp transform) will not break the ping-pong. => DEPRIORITIZE the Build-13 encoder pp transform as a loop fix; PIVOT to diagnosing/fixing the pp-independent ping-pong (localize its carrier a la Build 8, or a decision-time anti-repetition intervention / RL loop penalty, since imitation cannot fix an OOD 2-cycle absent from winning human play). BC 0.6236 (marginal) rules out shipping p 0.25 over p 0.10 as a milestone; p 0.10 (v11) remains the best BC-passing resample point."
}